  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The ions $\\mathrm{Ti}^{+2}, \\mathrm{~V}^{+2} \\mathrm{Cr}^{+2}$ are strong reducing agents and will liberate hydrogen from a dilute acid, eg.\n$2 \\mathrm{Cr}_{\\text {(aq.) }}^{+2}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{(\\text {aq.) }}^{+} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{Cr}_{(\\text {aq.) }}^{+3}+\\mathrm{H}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$",
